From fac03d05591316239a7814e6f0c4f96560861e17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shanks <shanks@book>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:59:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 25/37] feat(transportd): wire the X-CTD-Hookpoint switch (v1
 default)

Step-5 switch wiring only: v3 takes the same implementation path as v1 and
differs solely in its observation marker, so no body/header behavior changes.

- contract/headers.rs: parse `X-CTD-Hookpoint` as a closed set (v1|v3),
  missing = v1 (backward compatible with older Go), unknown value = typed
  contract error `invalid_hookpoint`, out-of-scope v3 = `invalid_hookpoint_scope`.
  Same shape as the existing `X-CTD-Proxy-Kind` handling, and both fire during
  admission, i.e. before any upstream I/O.
- build_info.rs: advertise `hookpoint_v1` / `hookpoint_v3` in /info CAPABILITIES.
- observability.rs: RequestObservation carries `hookpoint` and the requests_total
  key becomes `operation|hookpoint|outcome`.
- server/mod.rs: low-cardinality entry log in execute_operation_inner.

Tests: absent header = v1, explicit v1 is field-by-field equivalent to absent,
closed-set parse, invalid value, out-of-scope value, capability advertisement.
